// D-PERSIST1 — `#Persist` dev-hot-reload state survival.
// A module-level binding marked `#Persist` survives a `jet dev` hot reload
// instead of resetting (identity = module path + binding name + compatible
// shape). Release semantics are identical with or without the marker — this
// example documents the surface and its ordinary (non-dev) run: `#Persist` is
// inert here, so `counter` is simply its initial value.
//
// Dev-tier carry-across lives in the shared runtime-heap persist store
// (`jet_foundation::Persist`), consulted by both the interpreter and Cranelift
// tiers on hot-swap. See tests/dev.rs::persist_binding_survives_hot_swap_and_resets_on_shape_change.
#Persist const counter = 0

fn run() {
    print("{counter}")
}
// --- expected output --------------------------------------------------
// 0
